## THE DESIGN (the drafter's, decided at source and measured on scratch copies; every departure needs your written justification in STATUS)
**One product commit A445, `backend/marketplaceJwt.js` +30 -4 (a program: `diff -U0` hunks `@@ -63,0 +64,9 @@`, `@@ -99,0 +109,5 @@`, `@@ -101,0 +116,7 @@`, `@@ -113,4 +134,9 @@`; 138 to 164 lines; 5318 to 6602 bytes; non-ASCII bytes 24 before and 24 after, 0 CRLF; blob `d2feb537adac` to `8583d059c9b6`; `node --check` rc 0).** It adds two top-level helpers, a doc-comment paragraph, one log line when the router is built, and replaces the four-line bypass block at `:113` to `:117` with a branch that keeps the old three statements byte-for-byte (including the emoji and em dash line, only its indentation changes) for a non-production process and, in production, logs an error and falls through to the existing `try { validateMarketplaceToken ... }` block. **Nothing else changes.** `backend/server.js` and `marketplace-api.js` are not touched. **The frozen edit is this Python program** (the drafter's `apply1739.py`, ASCII, using `\u` escapes for the two non-ASCII characters of the old log line; every anchor asserted once; run it with two arguments, your clone's file and a temp file beside it, then `os.replace` the temp over the file; it prints the byte count, expected 6602):
```
import sys, os, hashlib
SRC=sys.argv[1]   # the clone's backend/marketplaceJwt.js at BASE
OUT=sys.argv[2]   # a temp file beside it; then os.replace it
b=open(SRC,'rb').read()
t=b.decode('utf-8')
def rep(t, old, new, n=1):
    assert t.count(old)==n, (old[:60], t.count(old))
    return t.replace(old,new)
# (1) two helpers after isAllowedIssuer, before the validateMarketplaceToken doc comment
anchor = "    return DEFAULT_ISSUERS.some(re => re.test(iss));\n}\n\n"
helpers = anchor + (
"// RD-445: the skip flag is read on every call, as before. In production it is never honoured.\n"
"function skipJwtFlagIsOn() {\n"
"    return String(process.env.MARKETPLACE_SKIP_JWT || '').toLowerCase() === 'true';\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"function isProductionEnv() {\n"
"    return String(process.env.NODE_ENV || '').trim().toLowerCase() === 'production';\n"
"}\n"
"\n")
t = rep(t, anchor, helpers)
# (2) doc comment
old_doc = " * The skip is logged loudly so a misconfigured production env is visible.\n */\n"
new_doc = (" * The skip is logged loudly so a misconfigured production env is visible.\n"
" *\n"
" * RD-445: when NODE_ENV=production the flag is NOT honoured. The token is\n"
" * verified exactly as if the flag were unset, and every request that meets\n"
" * the flag in production is logged at error level. The flag is not removed:\n"
" * development and sandbox runs still use it.\n"
" */\n")
t = rep(t, old_doc, new_doc)
# (3) factory-time line
old_fac = "function jwtMiddleware(opts = {}) {\n    return async (req, res, next) => {\n"
new_fac = ("function jwtMiddleware(opts = {}) {\n"
"    if (skipJwtFlagIsOn()) {\n"
"        if (isProductionEnv()) {\n"
"            logger.error('MARKETPLACE_SKIP_JWT=true is set while NODE_ENV=production: the flag is IGNORED and every webhook Bearer token is verified. Unset MARKETPLACE_SKIP_JWT.');\n"
"        } else {\n"
"            logger.warn('MARKETPLACE_SKIP_JWT=true is set: webhook Bearer tokens will NOT be verified in this process (not production).');\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"    return async (req, res, next) => {\n")
t = rep(t, old_fac, new_fac)
# (4) request-time branch
old_req = ("        if (String(process.env.MARKETPLACE_SKIP_JWT || '').toLowerCase() === 'true') {\n"
"            logger.warn('\u26a0\ufe0f  MARKETPLACE_SKIP_JWT=true \u2014 JWT validation BYPASSED. Do not run in production.');\n"
"            req.marketplaceTokenPayload = { iss: 'skipped', sub: 'skipped' };\n"
"            return next();\n"
"        }\n")
new_req = ("        if (skipJwtFlagIsOn()) {\n"
"            if (isProductionEnv()) {\n"
"                // RD-445: refused. Fall through to the verification below.\n"
"                logger.error('MARKETPLACE_SKIP_JWT=true was ignored for a webhook request because NODE_ENV=production: the Bearer token is being verified.');\n"
"            } else {\n"
"                logger.warn('\u26a0\ufe0f  MARKETPLACE_SKIP_JWT=true \u2014 JWT validation BYPASSED. Do not run in production.');\n"
"                req.marketplaceTokenPayload = { iss: 'skipped', sub: 'skipped' };\n"
"                return next();\n"
"            }\n"
"        }\n")
t = rep(t, old_req, new_req)
open(OUT,'wb').write(t.encode('utf-8'))
print('written',OUT,len(t.encode()),'bytes')
```
**The text it writes** (read it back from the file; do not retype it): helpers `skipJwtFlagIsOn()` (the old comparison, unchanged: `String(process.env.MARKETPLACE_SKIP_JWT || '').toLowerCase() === 'true'`) and `isProductionEnv()` (`String(process.env.NODE_ENV || '').trim().toLowerCase() === 'production'`); the factory logs `logger.error` in production and `logger.warn` otherwise when the flag is on; the request branch is `if (skipJwtFlagIsOn()) { if (isProductionEnv()) { logger.error(...) } else { <the three old statements> } }` and then the unchanged `try`. **The log lines are operator-facing, not customer-facing, and their exact words are a DEFAULT of this change (Q-4);** no customer-visible word is added (the 401 bodies `Invalid token`, `INVALID_TOKEN`, `INVALID_AUTH_HEADER` are unchanged); **if any added text would reach a browser or an API client, that is a STOP.** The three new log strings are ASCII, static, and name only the environment-variable names.
**Why these forms.** Production plus flag now behaves exactly as flag-off: the same `validateMarketplaceToken`, the same 401 on failure, the same `req.marketplaceTokenPayload` from the verified payload. The flag is read per request, as before, so a test or an operator changing it needs no restart. The request-time error line fires on every webhook request that meets the flag in production (the traffic is Microsoft's fulfilment webhooks, low volume); the factory line fires once per `jwtMiddleware()` call, which `marketplace-api.js` makes once when it builds its router, so a misconfigured instance is loud at boot before any request. **Not done (LEFT FOR OTHERS):** a boot refusal like `bootPreflight.js:131` (a `server.js` / `bootPreflight.js` change, other files), removal of the flag, any change to `scripts/test-marketplace-webhook.js`, `marketplace-api.js`, the audience constant (RD-415), and the other three items of RD-445.

